# Data conversion between mebibyte and petabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between mebibyte and petabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MiB to 0.0000PB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 0.0000PB; backward, converting 1PB to 953674316.4062MiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PB yields 1430511474.6093MiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(forward_whole->to(PB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(forward_fractional->to(PB))
backward_whole: int = 1PB
print(backward_whole->to(MiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PB
print(backward_fractional->to(MiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PB
0.0000PB
953674316.4062MiB
1430511474.6093MiB

<<< stderr
